KernelESP
=========

KernelESP is inspired by and contains source code copied/adapted from
KernelUNO, a lightweight UNIX-like shell for Arduino UNO created by Arc1011:

  https://github.com/Arc1011/KernelUNO

KernelUNO is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License. Source code portions
copied or adapted from KernelUNO remain credited to Arc1011 under that license.
KernelESP keeps the same BSD 3-Clause license family and acknowledges the
original project as both a conceptual and source-code starting point.

KernelESP is a substantial rework for ESP8266 with persistent LittleFS storage,
Wi-Fi, web UI, JSON API, automations, mail alerts, localized help, diagnostics
and release tooling.
